      "role": "user",
      "content": "right but if substantive due process is just \"making things up,\" then isn't the majority's version of originalism also just a way for them to pick and choose which history to use to get the outcome they want? it seems like both sides are just using different frameworks to justify their own views. isn't it more accurate to say there is no \"correct\" way, just different legal philosophies? or is one actually objectively better for the rule of law?",
